      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That drowning feeling is real, and it's okay to say it out loud—you don't have to pretend you're coping. The world moving on without him feels like a betrayal, but right now, you're allowed to stand still and feel every bit of the gray. Just surviving one breath at a time is enough; there is no \"should\" in grief. If the noise becomes too loud, maybe try putting on music he loved or writing him a messy note—not to feel better, just to let some of it out. And if you ever need to, you can tell me his name.",
